{"created": "2026-08-06T10:47:24.166244+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-06T10:47:25.328268+00:00", "id": 21822359, "conceptrecid": "21822358", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21822359", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21822358", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21822359", "metadata": {"title": "\u6ce2\u306e\u5468\u671f\u8868\u2014\u2014\u5dfb\u304d\u6570\u756a\u5730\u3068\u89b3\u6e2c\u6642\u8a08\u306b\u3088\u308b\u7c92\u5b50\u5206\u985e\u306e\u4eee\u8aac / The Periodic Table of Waves: A Hypothesis for Particle Classification by Winding Addresses and Observation Clocks", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21822359", "publication_date": "2026-08-06", "description": "A hypothesis-proposal paper: particle species are classified not as fixed attributes of waves but by how an observation clock reads winding states \u2014 decomposing charge, confinement, statistics, mass, and lifetime into (state-side address) x (observation clock) x (relation to the sea). Built purely from measurements on two published anonymous wave dynamics: universal clock omega=pi/72 (N=4-144, 0.1%), charge rule Q_em=m/3 with confinement = mod-3 readability (isolated quark-type windings remain exactly unreadable; hadronization restores integer charge), statistics = Z2 clock double cover (phase quantized to {0,pi}), mass as a relation to the sea (divisor-class theorem), and a native periodic table with a 62-species Standard-Model assignment (confidence-tagged). Includes 13 recorded refutations, 5 falsification conditions, and the requirement specification for a unifying universal interaction function. \u4eee\u8aac\u63d0\u6848\u8ad6\u6587\u3002\u7c92\u5b50\u7a2e\u3092\u6ce2\u306e\u56fa\u5b9a\u5c5e\u6027\u3067\u306f\u306a\u304f\u300c\u72b6\u614b\u5074\u306e\u756a\u5730\u00d7\u89b3\u6e2c\u6642\u8a08\u00d7\u6d77\u3068\u306e\u95a2\u4fc2\u300d\u3067\u5206\u985e\u3059\u308b\u3002\u666e\u904d\u6642\u8a08\u03c9=\u03c0/72\u3001\u96fb\u8377\u5247Q_em=m/3\u3068\u9589\u3058\u8fbc\u3081=mod3\u53ef\u8aad\u6027\u3001\u7d71\u8a08=Z\u2082\u6642\u8a08\u88ab\u8986\u3001\u8cea\u91cf=\u6d77\u3068\u306e\u95a2\u4fc2\u91cf\u3001\u539f\u59cb\u5468\u671f\u8868\u3068\u6a19\u6e96\u6a21\u578b62\u7a2e\u5272\u5f53\u6848(\u78ba\u5ea6\u8a18\u53f7\u4ed8\u304d)\u3002\u53cd\u8a3c13\u4ef6\u30fb\u53cd\u8a3c\u6761\u4ef65\u4ef6\u30fb\u4e07\u80fd\u76f8\u4e92\u4f5c\u7528\u95a2\u6570\u3078\u306e\u8981\u4ef6\u4ed5\u69d8\u3092\u542b\u3080\u3002", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kihara, Noriaki", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["particle classification", "winding number", "observation clock", "charge quantization", "confinement", "spin-statistics", "double cover", "emergent particles", "wave dynamics", "periodic table"], "language": "jpn", "license": "cc-by-4.0", "imprint_publisher": "Zenodo", "upload_type": "publication", "publication_type": "preprint", "prereserve_doi": {"doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21822359", "recid": 21822359}}, "title": "\u6ce2\u306e\u5468\u671f\u8868\u2014\u2014\u5dfb\u304d\u6570\u756a\u5730\u3068\u89b3\u6e2c\u6642\u8a08\u306b\u3088\u308b\u7c92\u5b50\u5206\u985e\u306e\u4eee\u8aac / The Periodic Table of Waves: A Hypothesis for Particle Classification by Winding Addresses and Observation Clocks", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21822359", "html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21822359", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21822359", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21822358", "badge": "https://zenodo.org/badge/doi/10.5281%2Fzenodo.21822359.svg", "conceptbadge": "https://zenodo.org/badge/doi/10.5281%2Fzenodo.21822358.svg", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21822359/files", "bucket": "https://zenodo.org/api/files/e253beee-6253-4184-88f6-d5252d593f37", "thumb250": "https://zenodo.org/record/21822359/thumb250", "thumbs": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/record/21822359/thumb10", "50": "https://zenodo.org/record/21822359/thumb50", "100": "https://zenodo.org/record/21822359/thumb100", "250": "https://zenodo.org/record/21822359/thumb250", "750": "https://zenodo.org